name: canon-boundary
kind: inferred
shape: categorical
face: in
membrane: true
note: a commit reclassifies a field or construct across the canon
  trivia boundary — what serializeCanon counts as "same program" vs
  "same spelling". Fires when isTrivia gains or loses a field
  (location/indent/had_explicit_label today), when the printer's
  normalization choices change what provenance can survive a
  print→reparse, or when a tree-diff class turns out to be spelling
  rather than semantics. The signal exists because the round-trip
  harness's pass rate is only meaningful if canon strips exactly the
  provenance and nothing else — every reclassification moves hundreds
  of corpus diffs at once (had_explicit_label alone was 1212).
